course: dictionary
lesson: 3086
title: Edwardian
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Edwardian is a word about time. It describes things from the time when Edward VII was king of the United Kingdom, from 1901 to 1910. Some historians stretch it to 1914, just before the First World War. «The Wind in the Willows» came out in 1908, when King Edward VII was on the throne, so that time is called the Edwardian age.
explain: Edwardian can also be a noun. An Edwardian is a person who lived in that time, and Edwardians means the people of that time.
explain: Edwardian can describe a style too. Clothes, houses and furniture made in that time can be Edwardian. Edwardian houses often have bay windows and big gardens. You can say «an Edwardian house» or «Edwardian England».
explain: Use the context to check. In «The Wind in the Willows», Toad's motor cars, gramophones and picnics all belong to the Edwardian era. Those clues tell you what kind of time the word means.
fact: Edwardian comes from Edward, the name of King Edward VII.
fact: The Edwardian era is the reign of King Edward VII, from 1901 to 1910.
fact: In history lessons, the Edwardian era follows the Victorian era.
fact: «The Wind in the Willows» by Kenneth Grahame was published in 1908, so it is an Edwardian book.
fact: Edwardian can be an adjective, as in «an Edwardian house», or a noun, as in «an Edwardian», a person who lived in that time.
exercise: «The Wind in the Willows» came out in 1908, when King Edward VII was on the throne. Which era does this mean? | The Victorian era | The Roman era | The Tudor era | *The Edwardian era
exercise: What does Edwardian describe in «an Edwardian house with a bay window»? | A Scottish word for rain | *A style typical of that time | A kind of food | A sports team
exercise: Which years does the Edwardian era cover? | *1901 to 1910 | 1837 to 1901 | 1914 to 1918 | 1066 to 1087
test: Toad's motor cars and gramophones belong to which time? | Stone Age | Medieval | Victorian | *Edwardian
test: What do we call a person who lived in the Edwardian era? | A Tudor | *An Edwardian | Victorian | A Roman
exam: Which statement is true? | Edwardian means a Scottish word for rain | *Edwardian England follows Victorian England in history lessons | An Edwardian house always has a small garden and no windows | The Edwardian era is the reign of Queen Victoria
